</section>

</div><div class='sfContentBlock'><div class="first-fold-wrap">
    <section class="section-content read-more-cont" id="car-ins">
        <div class="il-container">
            <div class="img-cont-sec">
                <div class="cont-sec">
                    <h2 class="heading2 mb-20">What is Car Insurance?</h2>
                    <p class="text">Your car is more than just a machine, it’s your companion on every journey, and it deserves reliable protection. Our car insurance acts as a dependable shield, covering you against unexpected events such as accidents, theft, and natural disasters, while also ensuring you stay compliant with the Motor Vehicles Act, 1988, which makes third-party insurance mandatory. </p>
                    <p class="text mt-20">With policy starting at just ₹2094 per year<sup>B</sup>, you enjoy the peace of mind that comes with cashless repairs at trusted network garages, hassle-free claim settlement, and 24x7 customer support. Wherever the road takes you, drive with confidence knowing we’re always by your side. </p>
                  
                 
                </div>
                <div class="img-sec">
                    <img data-src="/docs/default-source/assets/marketing/images/motor-fw-revamp/what_is_car_insurance.webp" alt="What Is Car Insurance?" title="What Is Car Insurance?" class="lazy tw-ins-img" width="399">
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section-content quick-sum-block" id="quick-sum">
        <div class="il-container quick-block">
            <div class="flex-block">
                <img data-src="/docs/default-source/assets/marketing/images/health-revamp/ai-ico.webp" alt="Quick summary" title="Quick summary" class="lazy">
                <h2 class="heading2 align-center">Quick Summary</h2>
            </div>
            <div class="arrow-list mt-40">
                <ul class="list list2">
                    <li class="list-item">
                        <p class="text">Car insurance protects your vehicle against damages and losses caused by accidents, theft, natural and man-made calamities, fire, third-party liabilities, etc. </p>
                    </li>
                    <li class="list-item">
                        <p class="text">It is mandatory to have third-party car insurance to legally drive your vehicle on Indian roads. </p>
                    </li>
                    <li class="list-item">
                        <p class="text">You can opt for add-ons like Zero Depreciation Cover, Consumable Items Cover, IL Smart Assist, Engine Protect Plus, Pay As You Drive and more to customise your car insurance coverage.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li class="list-item">
                        <p class="text">Your car insurance premium is based on your vehicle’s IDV, fuel type, make and model, age, geography, claim history and add-ons opted. </p>
                    </li>
                    <li class="list-item">
                        <p class="text">You can earn a No Claim Bonus of up to 50% for not making any claims in five consecutive years.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li class="list-item">
                        <p class="text">You need to renew your car insurance policy on time to retain your accumulated NCB, avoid a policy lapse, meet legal requirements and enjoy continuous coverage.</p>
                    </li>
                </ul>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section-content bg-sec-blue owl-div" id="why-car-insu-mandatory">
        <div class="il-container">
            <h2 class="heading2 align-center">Why is Car Insurance Mandatory in India?</h2>
            <p class="text sub-txt mt-30 align-center mid-width">You need to have at least a third-party car insurance to drive a vehicle on public roads. It is a legal requirement under the Motor Vehicles Act, 1988. You can face fines up to ₹2000 and ₹4000 for subsequent offenses and/or imprisonment for
                upto three months for driving without a valid insurance.</p>
            <div class="col-wrap owl-carousel owl-theme owl-sec mt-30">
                <div class="col-item">
                    <img alt="Car Insurance - Third-Party Protection" title="Car Insurance - Third-Party Protection" class="lazy" data-src="/docs/default-source/assets/marketing/images/motor-fw-revamp/third_party_protection.webp">
                    <div class="col-content typesof-tw">
                        <h3 class="heading3">Third-Party Protection</h3>
                        <p class="text color-coolgray mt-10">Accidents don’t just impact you. They can also affect pedestrians, passengers and other vehicles. A <a href="/motor-insurance/car-insurance/third-party-car-insurance" target="_blank" class="link"> third-party car insurance</a> helps to compensate those affected by your insured vehicle.</p>

                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="col-item">
                    <img alt="Car Insurance - Legally Mandatory" title="Car Insurance - Legally Mandatory" class="lazy " data-src="/docs/default-source/assets/marketing/images/motor-fw-revamp/legal_compliance.webp">
                    <div class="col-content typesof-tw">
                        <h3 class="heading3 ">Legal Compliance</h3>
                        <p class="text color-coolgray mt-10">As per the Motor Vehicles Act, 1988, every vehicle owner must have at least a third-party car insurance policy to drive legally on Indian roads. Driving without valid insurance can attract fines, penalties, and even imprisonment as prescribed under the law.</p>

                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="col-item">
                    <img alt="Accident Rates - Prepare Before Hand " title="Accident Rates - Prepare Before Hand" class="lazy" data-src="/docs/default-source/assets/marketing/images/motor-fw-revamp/high_accident_rates.webp">
                    <div class="col-content typesof-tw">
                        <h3 class="heading3">High Accident Rates </h3>
                        <p class="text color-coolgray mt-10">With a significant number of road accidents reported every year across the country, the risk of unforeseen incidents remains high. Car insurance offers financial protection against the expenses that may arise from accidents, helping vehicle owners manage risks effectively. </p>

                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="col-item">
                    <img alt="Car Insurance Handles Unexpected Expenses " title="Car Insurance Handles Unexpected Expenses " class="lazy" data-src="/docs/default-source/assets/marketing/images/motor-fw-revamp/financial-risks.webp">
                    <div class="col-content typesof-tw">
                        <h3 class="heading3">Protection Against Financial Losses</h3>
                        <p class="text color-coolgray mt-10">Repairing damaged vehicles, replacing parts, or paying legal compensation following an accident can be expensive. Car insurance helps cover these unexpected costs, reducing the financial burden on vehicle owners.</p>

                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section-content bg-warmgray tab-wrap" id="car-cover">
        <div class="il-container">
            <h2 class="heading2 align-center inclusive-head">What is Covered Under Car Insurance?</h2>
            <h2 class="heading2 align-center exclusive-head" style="display:none;">What is Not Covered Under Car Insurance?</h2>


            <p class="sub-txt align-center mid-width inclusive-para width-80">The best car insurance does more than just meet legal requirements — it protects you from unexpected expenses. Understanding what your policy covers helps you know exactly when and how you’re protected. Here are some key inclusions of ICICI
                Lombard car insurance:</p>

            <p class="sub-txt align-center mid-width exclusive-para width-80" style="display:none;">While the right car insurance offers wide protection, it doesn’t cover everything. Knowing what’s excluded helps you avoid surprises at the time of a claim. Here’s a simple look at what is not covered under a car insurance policy.</p>

            <div class="tab-block">
                <div class="tab-sec">
                    <ul>
                        <li class="active" data-rel="inclusion"><span>What’s Covered </span>
                        </li>
                        <li data-rel="exclusion" class=""><span>What’s Not Covered </span>
                        </li>
                    </ul>
                </div>
                <div class="tab-data">
                    <div class="tab-cont active read-more-option" id="inclusion">
                        <ul class="list-block check-list2 grid-list">
                            <li class="flex-list">
                                <h4 class="heading4">Accidental Damages</h4>
                                <p class="text">Unexpected collisions, road accidents, and impacts can result in costly repairs. Car insurance helps cover damages or losses to your insured vehicle caused by accidents.</p>
                            </li>
                            <li class="flex-list">
                                <h4 class="heading4">Theft</h4>
                                <p class="text">If your insured car is stolen, you can receive compensation based on the vehicle's Insured Declared Value (IDV), subject to policy terms and conditions.</p>
                            </li>
                            <li class="flex-list">
                                <h4 class="heading4">Fire-Related Damage</h4>
                                <p class="text">Your policy provides coverage for losses or damages caused by fire, self-ignition, explosion, lightning, and similar fire-related incidents.</p>
                            </li>
                            <li class="flex-list">
                                <h4 class="heading4">Natural Calamities</h4>
                                <p class="text">Stay protected against damage caused by natural events such as floods, earthquakes, cyclones, storms, typhoons, landslides, and other natural disasters.</p>
                            </li>
                            <li class="flex-list more-option-show">
                                <h4 class="heading4">Man-made Disasters</h4>
                                <p class="text">Coverage extends to damages resulting from riots, strikes, vandalism, malicious acts, and terrorist activities, as specified in the policy.</p>
                            </li>
                            <li class="flex-list more-option-show">
                                <h4 class="heading4">Personal Accident Cover</h4>
                                <p class="text">Owner-drivers are covered in the unfortunate event of accidental death or permanent disability, with compensation of up to ₹15 lakh as per policy provisions.</p>
                            </li>
                            <li class="flex-list more-option-show">
                                <h4 class="heading4">Third-party Liabilities</h4>
                                <p class="text">Comprehensive car insurance also covers legal liabilities arising from injuries, death, or property damage caused to third parties due to an accident involving your insured vehicle. </p>
                            </li>
                            <li class="flex-list more-option-show">
                                <h4 class="heading4">Damages During Transit</h4>
                                <p class="text">Your vehicle is protected against loss or damage that may occur while being transported by road, rail, inland waterways, air, or lift. </p>
                            </li>

                        </ul>
                        <a role="button" class="read-more-opt-btn">Read more</a>
                        <p class="note-txt">Note: This is an indicative list. Kindly go through the policy wordings for detailed information on car insurance inclusions. </p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="tab-cont read-more-option" id="exclusion">
                        <ul class="list-block cross-list grid-list">
                            <li class="flex-list">
                                <h4 class="heading4">Damage Outside the Geographical Limits</h4>
                                <p class="text">Losses or damages occurring when the vehicle is driven or used outside India are not covered under the policy.</p>
                            </li>
                            <li class="flex-list">
                                <h4 class="heading4">Normal Wear and Tear</h4>
                                <p class="text">Routine deterioration due to ageing, regular usage, depreciation, or gradual wear and tear of vehicle components is not covered.</p>
                            </li>
                            <li class="flex-list">
                                <h4 class="heading4">Consequential loss</h4>
                                <p class="text">Any loss or damage arising due to negligence, delayed action, or continued use of a damaged vehicle may not be admissible under the policy.</p>
                            </li>
                            <li class="flex-list ">
                                <h4 class="heading4">War and Nuclear Risks</h4>
                                <p class="text">Damages caused directly or indirectly by war, invasion, civil war, rebellion, nuclear risks, or warlike operations are excluded.</p>
                            </li>
                            <li class="flex-list more-option-show">
                                <h4 class="heading4">Illegal Driving</h4>
                                <p class="text">Claims may be rejected if the vehicle is being driven under the influence of alcohol or drugs, by a person without a valid driving licence, or in violation of applicable laws.</p>
                            </li>
                            <li class="flex-list more-option-show">
                                <h4 class="heading4">Mechanical or Electrical Breakdown</h4>
                                <p class="text">Losses resulting solely from mechanical, electrical, or electronic failures and breakdowns are not covered unless specifically mentioned under an add-on cover.</p>
                            </li>

                        </ul>

                        <a role="button" class="read-more-opt-btn">Read more</a>
                        <p class="note-txt">Note: This is an indicative list of exclusions. Please refer to the policy wordings for a comprehensive understanding of all exclusions, conditions, and limitations under the car insurance policy.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>



            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section-content read-more-option flex-wrap" id="how-to-choose-right-car">
        <div class="il-container">
            <h2 class="heading2 align-center">How to Choose the Right Car Insurance Policy? </h2>
            <p class="sub-txt color-coolgray align-center mid-width">Selecting the right car insurance policy is an important step towards protecting your vehicle and finances. From understanding coverage options to evaluating your driving needs, a few key considerations can help you make an informed decision. Here are some factors to keep in mind when choosing the best car insurance policy for your car:</p>
            <div class="row-block mt-20">
                <div class="row-item">
                    <div class="img-wrap"><img data-src="/docs/default-source/assets/marketing/images/motor-fw-revamp/choose_the_right_coverage.webp" alt="Choose the Right Coverage " title="Choose the Right Coverage " class="lazy">
                    </div>
                    <div class="row-cont">
                        <h3 class="heading3">Choose the Right Coverage </h3>
                        <p class="text mt-10">Start by identifying the level of protection you require. While third-party car insurance is mandatory by law, you may want to consider own damage or <a target="_blank" href="/motor-insurance/car-insurance/comprehensive-car-insurance" class="link">  comprehensive car insurance</a> for wider coverage against accidents, theft, natural calamities, and other risks.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="row-item">
                    <div class="img-wrap"><img data-src="/docs/default-source/assets/marketing/images/motor-fw-revamp/choose_the_right_idv.webp" alt="Choose the Right IDV" title="Choose the Right IDV" class="lazy ">
                    </div>
                    <div class="row-cont">
                        <h3 class="heading3">Opt for an Appropriate IDV</h3>
                        <p class="text mt-10">The Insured Declared Value (IDV) represents the maximum amount payable in case of total loss or theft of your vehicle. Choosing an appropriate IDV can help ensure adequate financial protection during major claims.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="row-item">
                    <div class="img-wrap"><img data-src="/docs/default-source/assets/marketing/images/motor-fw-revamp/evaluate_your_driving_style.webp" alt="Evaluate Your Driving Style" title="Evaluate Your Driving Style" class="lazy ">
                    </div>
                    <div class="row-cont">
                        <h3 class="heading3">Assess Your Driving Habits</h3>
                        <p class="text mt-10">How often and how far you drive can influence the type of policy that best suits your needs. If your vehicle usage is limited, you may explore flexible options such as Pay As You Drive or Pay How You Drive plans.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="row-item more-option-show">
                    <div class="img-wrap"><img data-src="/docs/default-source/assets/marketing/images/motor-fw-revamp/decide_your_risk_appetite.webp" alt="Decide Your Comfort with Risk" title="Decide Your Comfort with Risk" class="lazy ">
                    </div>
                    <div class="row-cont">
                        <h3 class="heading3">Consider Your Risk Appetite </h3>
                        <p class="text mt-10">Evaluate how much out-of-pocket expense you would be comfortable bearing in the event of vehicle damage. If you prefer broader financial protection, a comprehensive policy with suitable add-on covers may be a worthwhile choice.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="row-item more-option-show">
                    <div class="img-wrap"><img data-src="/docs/default-source/assets/marketing/images/motor-fw-revamp/consider_your_location.webp" alt="Consider Your Location" title="Consider Your Location" class="lazy ">
                    </div>
                    <div class="row-cont">
                        <h3 class="heading3">Factor in Your Location</h3>
                        <p class="text mt-10">The area where your vehicle is primarily used or parked can impact insurance premiums. Factors such as traffic density, accident frequency, and vehicle theft rates may influence the overall risk and cost of insurance.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="row-item more-option-show">
                    <div class="img-wrap"><img data-src="/docs/default-source/assets/marketing/images/motor-fw-revamp/check_for_discounts.webp" alt="Check for Discounts" title="Check for Discounts" class="lazy ">
                    </div>
                    <div class="row-cont">
                        <h3 class="heading3">Check for Discounts  </h3>
                        <p class="text mt-10">Look for discounts you might be eligible for, such as discounts for having multiple policies, being a safe driver, driving less or opting for a multi-tenure policy.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <a role="button" class="read-more-opt-btn">Read more</a>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section-content bg-pink" id="thing-to-do-mind">
        <div class="il-container">
            <h2 class="heading2 align-center">Things to Keep in Mind While Buying Car Insurance</h2>

            <div class="flex-div mt-40 read-more-list">
                <div class="list-block org-list width-equal org-list-block">
                    <ul>
                        <li>
                            <h4 class="heading4">Understand Policy Coverage</h4>
                            <p class="text">Review the policy’s inclusions and exclusions to understand what is covered and what is not. Choosing a policy only on the basis of price may not provide the level of protection you need. All coverage is subject to policy terms and conditions.</p>
                        </li>
                        <li>
                            <h4 class="heading4">Choose Useful Add-ons<sup>G</sup></h4>
                            <p class="text">Add-ons serve specific purposes and may help enhance coverage based on your requirements. Assess them carefully and select only those that are relevant for your vehicle and usage. Add-ons are optional and available at an additional premium.</p>
                        </li>
                        <li>
                            <h4 class="heading4">Review Service Quality</h4>
                            <p class="text">Check whether the insurer offers a wide network of <a class="link" target="_blank" href="/cashless-garages">cashless garages</a>, a straightforward claims process, and accessible customer support. These aspects can support smoother assistance during claim situations.</p>
                        </li>

                    </ul>
                </div>
                <div class="list-block org-list width-equal org-list-block">
                    <ul>
                        <li>
                            <h4 class="heading4">Select an Appropriate IDV</h4>
                            <p class="text">A lower Insured Declared Value (IDV) may reduce the premium but can also reduce the claim amount. It is advisable to choose an IDV that reflects your car’s current market value for balanced coverage.</p>
                        </li>
                        <li>
                            <h4 class="heading4">Understand Deductibles</h4>
                            <p class="text">A higher deductible lowers the premium but increases the amount you pay during a claim. A lower deductible increases the premium. Choose a deductible level that aligns with your comfort and financial readiness.</p>
                        </li>

                    </ul>
                </div>
                <!-- <a role="button" class="read-more-link">Read more</a> -->
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section-content " id="zero-deprecation-car">
        <div class="il-container">
            <h2 class="heading2 align-center">What is IDV (Insured Declared Value)?</h2>
            <p class="sub-txt width-90 mt-20 align-center">The <a href="https://www.icicilombard.com/motor-insurance/car-insurance/idv-in-car-insurance" title="" class="link" target="">Insured’s Declared Value (IDV) in car insurance </a>is the approximate value of your car in the market today. It is also the maximum amount your insurer may pay if your car is stolen or damaged beyond repair, as per the policy terms and conditions.</p>
            <p class="sub-txt width-90 mt-10 align-center">To put it simply, IDV is the current value of your car after deducting depreciation.</p>

            <p class="sub-txt width-90 mt-15 align-center strong-txt">IDV = Manufacturer's listed selling price + Listed cost of accessories - Depreciation </p>

            <p class="sub-txt mt-20 align-center">Depreciation is calculated using standard rates defined under the Indian Motor Tariff. These rates help estimate how much your car’s value has reduced over time, so the IDV stays fair and realistic.</p>
            <div class="table-wrapper table-style1  width-85 mt-30">
                <table class="table-wrap">
                    <thead>
                        <tr>
                            <th style="width: 50%">Age of Your Car</th>
                            <th style="width: 50%">Applicable Percentage of Depreciation </th>
                        </tr>
                    </thead>
                    <tbody>

                        <tr>
                            <td class="strong-txt" style="width: 50%">Not more than 6 months</td>
                            <td style="width: 50%">5%</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td class="strong-txt">More than 6 months but less than 1 year</td>
                            <td>15%</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td class="strong-txt">More than 1 year but less than 2 years</td>
                            <td>20%</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td class="strong-txt">More than 2 years but less than 3 years</td>
                            <td>30%</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td class="strong-txt">More than 3 years but less than 4 years</td>
                            <td>40%</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td class="strong-txt">More than 4 years but less than 5 years</td>
                            <td>50%</td>
                        </tr>

                    </tbody>
                </table>
            </div>
            <div class="width-90">
                <p class="align-center mt-20 sub-txt">Let’s understand this with an example. Suppose the listed selling price of your vehicle was ₹4,00,000 and you added accessories worth ₹50,000. The total value of your car would be ₹4,50,000. And the applicable depreciation after two years
                    would be ₹90,000 (which is 20% of ₹4,50,000). As a result, your IDV would be ₹4,50,000 - ₹90,000 = ₹3,60,000.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section-content owl-div bg-sec-blue which-factor" id="Which-Factors-Affect-car-Premium">
        <div class="il-container read-more-option">
            <h2 class="heading2 align-center">Which Factors Affect Your Car Insurance Premium?</h2>
            <p class="text align-center">Car insurance premium is calculated based on a number of factors and components. These decide how much risk your car carries and, in turn, your final premium amount.</p>
            <div class="option-block ">
                <div class="option-item">
                    <h3 class="heading3">Coverage Type </h3>
                    <p class="text">Your car insurance premium is based on the type of policy you choose. The premium for third-party car insurance is lower than a comprehensive car insurance.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="option-item">
                    <h3 class="heading3">IDV </h3>
                    <p class="text">IDV in car insurance plays a key role in determining your payable premium. The higher your car’s market value, the higher your IDV and premium will
                        be. </p>
                </div>
                <div class="option-item ">
                    <h3 class="heading3">Make and Model </h3>
                    <p class="text">Luxury and higher-end car models are typically insured at a higher price, simply because the cost of repairs/replacement for such vehicles is higher.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="option-item ">
                    <h3 class="heading3">Fuel Type</h3>
                    <p class="text">Repairing petrol-fuelled cars is cheaper than those that run on diesel and CNG. As a result, they are also less expensive to insure.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="option-item more-option-show">
                    <h3 class="heading3">Year of Manufacture</h3>
                    <p class="text">Both new and older cars can be costly to insure since their spare parts are hard to find in the market. </p>
                </div>
                <div class="option-item more-option-show">
                    <h3 class="heading3">Location </h3>
                    <p class="text">There’s a greater probability of accidental damages in urban areas since they tend to have denser traffic. Thus, your premium may vary depending on your location.</p>
                </div>

                <div class="option-item more-option-show">
                    <h3 class="heading3">Claim history</h3>
                    <p class="text"> You can gain up to 50% NCB on your premium if you didn’t file any car insurance claims in the last five years.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="option-item more-option-show">
                    <h3 class="heading3">Add-ons </h3>
                    <p class="text">You can opt for optional covers like <a class="link" target="_blank" href="/motor-insurance/car-insurance/zero-depreciation-car-insurance">Zero Depreciation Cover in Car Insurance</a> , <a class="link" target="_blank" href="/motor-insurance/car-insurance/engine-protect-insurance">Engine Protect Cover in Car Insurance</a>, etc</p>
                </div>
            </div>
            <a role="button" class="read-more-opt-btn">Read more</a>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section-content how-to-cal" id="how-to-calculate-premium-online">
        <div class="il-container">
            <h2 class="heading2 align-center">How to Calculate Car Insurance Premium Online? </h2>
            <p class="sub-txt color-coolgray align-center mid-width">Before you buy your car insurance online, you need to understand how your premium is calculated. Did you know that your car insurance premium includes three major components? Yes, that’s right. These components include the third-party insurance
                premium, own damage insurance premium, and personal accident cover + add-on premium.</p>
           <div class="row-block mt-20">
                 <div class="row-item-wrapper">
                    <div class="row-table-indi">
                      <div class="row-img-con-wrapper">
                          <div class="img-wrap"><img data-src="/docs/default-source/assets/marketing/images/motor-fw-revamp/third_party_liability_premium.webp" alt="Third-party Liability Premium " title="Third-party Liability Premium " class="lazy ">
                        </div>
                        <div class="row-cont">
                            <h3 class="heading3">Third-party Liability Premium </h3>
                            <p class="text mt-10">This is directly proportional to your car’s cubic capacity. The rates are stipulated
                                by the Insurance Regulatory and Development Authority of India (IRDAI).</p>
                        </div>
                      </div>
                        <!-- <div class="how-to-cal-wrapper">
                            <div class="table-wrapper table-style1  width-85 mt-30 how-to-cal-table">
                                <table class="table-wrap">
                                    <thead>
                                        <tr>
                                            <th style="width: 50%">Car’s Cubic Capacity (CC)</th>
                                            <th style="width: 50%">Third-party Insurance Premium</th>
                                        </tr>
                                    </thead>
                                    <tbody>
                                        <tr>
                                            <td class="strong-txt" style="width: 50%">Less than 1000 CC</td>
                                            <td style="width: 50%">₹2,094</td>
                                        </tr>
                                        <tr>
                                            <td class="strong-txt" style="width: 50%">More than 1000 CC but less than 1500 CC</td>
                                            <td style="width: 50%">₹3,416</td>
                                        </tr>
                                        <tr>
                                            <td class="strong-txt">More than 1500 CC</td>
                                            <td>₹7,897</td>
                                        </tr>
                
                                    </tbody>
                                </table>
                            </div>
                        </div> -->
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="row-item-wrapper"><div class="row-img-con-wrapper">
                    <div class="img-wrap"><img data-src="/docs/default-source/assets/marketing/images/motor-fw-revamp/own_damage_premium.webp" alt="Own Damage Premium" title="Own Damage Premium" class="lazy ">
                    </div>
                    <div class="row-cont">
                        <h3 class="heading3">Own Damage Premium </h3>
                        <p class="text mt-10">This is calculated based on factors such as car value, age, location, claim history and selected add-ons. The formula to calculate your Own Damage Premium1 is: IDV x [Tariff Rate] – [Discounts] </p>
                    </div></div>
                </div>
                <div class="row-item-wrapper"><div class="row-img-con-wrapper">
                    <div class="img-wrap"><img data-src="/docs/default-source/assets/marketing/images/motor-fw-revamp/personal_accident_cover_premium.webp" alt="Personal Accident Cover Premium + Add-on Covers" title="Personal Accident Cover Premium + Add-on Covers" class="lazy ">
                    </div>
                    <div class="row-cont">
                        <h3 class="heading3">Personal Accident Cover Premium + Add-on Covers  </h3>
                        <p class="text mt-10">This includes the Personal Accident Cover for the owner-driver and any optional covers you choose. These can be added to your base coverage for a nominal cost.</p>
                    </div></div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <p class="text align-center mt-20 how-to-cal-para">Besides this, you can also use our <a href="/motor-insurance/car-insurance/car-insurance-calculator" class="link" target="_blank">car insurance premium calculator</a> to easily know your payable premium. </p>

            <p class="text align-center mt-20">Note: 1: The payable OD premium is also subject to policy terms and conditions.</p>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section-content owl-div bg-pink" id="how-to-get-car-quote-online">
        <div class="il-container">
            <h2 class="heading2 align-center">How to Find the Best Car Insurance Quote Online? </h2>
            <p class="text align-center">Finding the right car insurance quote online becomes easier when you know what to look for. Here are a few points that can help you make an informed choice, while keeping everything aligned with policy terms and conditions.</p>
            <div class="grad-block">
                <div class="grad-sec ">
                    <div class="grad-item">
                        <div class="ico-block">
                            <img data-src="/docs/default-source/assets/marketing/images/motor-fw-revamp/know_your_insurer_s_network_strength.webp" alt="Insurer’s Network Strength" title="Insurer’s Network Strength" class="lazy ">
                        </div>
                        <div class="grad-cont">
                            <h3 class="heading3">Check the Insurer’s Cashless Garage Network</h3>
                            <p class="text">See whether the insurer offers a wide network of cashless garages. A larger network can help you access repair services more smoothly during a claim.</p>

                            <!-- <a href="https://www.icicilombard.com/health-insurance/elevate-health-policy?opt=elevate&amp;source=nav" class="know-more-link" target="_blank">Know More</a> -->
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="grad-item">
                        <div class="ico-block">
                            <img data-src="/docs/default-source/assets/marketing/images/motor-fw-revamp/check_what_customers_are_saying.webp" alt="Check What Customers Are Saying " title="Check What Customers Are Saying" class="lazy ">
                        </div>
                        <div class="grad-cont">
                            <h3 class="heading3">Read Customer Feedback</h3>
                            <p class="text">Customer reviews can give you an idea of service quality, claim handling, and overall experience. This helps set realistic expectations.</p>

                            <!-- <a href="https://www.icicilombard.com/health-insurance/health-booster?opt=ab&amp;source=nav" class="know-more-link" target="_blank">Know More</a> -->
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="grad-item">
                        <div class="ico-block">
                            <img data-src="/docs/default-source/assets/marketing/images/motor-fw-revamp/understand_the_claims_process.webp" alt="Understand the Claims Process" title="Understand the Claims Process" class="lazy ">
                        </div>
                        <div class="grad-cont">
                            <h3 class="heading3">Understand the Claims Process </h3>
                            <p class="text">Review how simple and transparent the claims process is. A clear process can reduce confusion during stressful situations.</p>

                            <!-- <a href="https://www.icicilombard.com/health-insurance/activate-booster-combo?opt=abcartemis&amp;source=nav" class="know-more-link" target="_blank">Know More</a> -->
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="grad-item">
                        <div class="ico-block">
                            <img data-src="/docs/default-source/assets/marketing/images/motor-fw-revamp/look_at_the_claim_settlement_ratio.webp" alt="Check the Claim Settlement Ratio" title="Check the Claim Settlement Ratio" class="lazy ">
                        </div>
                        <div class="grad-cont">
                            <h3 class="heading3">Check the Claim Settlement Ratio</h3>
                            <p class="text">The claim settlement ratio indicates how many valid claims the insurer has settled. It can help you assess reliability, but should be considered along with other factors.</p>

                            <!-- <a href="https://www.icicilombard.com/health-insurance/max-protect-1-crore-health-insurance?opt=max&amp;source=nav" class="know-more-link" target="_blank">Know More</a> -->
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="grad-item">
                        <div class="ico-block">
                            <img data-src="/docs/default-source/assets/marketing/images/motor-fw-revamp/compare_policies_based_on_benefits.webp" alt="Compare Policies Based on Benefits" title="Compare Policies Based on Benefits" class="lazy ">
                        </div>
                        <div class="grad-cont">
                            <h3 class="heading3">Compare Policies Carefull</h3>
                            <p class="text">Do not rely on the first quote you receive. Compare coverage options, add-ons, and policy features to choose a plan that matches your needs.</p>

                            <!-- <a href="https://www.icicilombard.com/health-insurance/max-protect-1-crore-health-insurance?opt=max&amp;source=nav" class="know-more-link" target="_blank">Know More</a> -->
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="grad-item">
                        <div class="ico-block">
                            <img data-src="/docs/default-source/assets/marketing/images/motor-fw-revamp/look_for_available_discounts.webp" alt="Check Available Discounts " title="Check Available Discounts " class="lazy ">
                        </div>
                        <div class="grad-cont">
                            <h3 class="heading3">Check for Available Discounts</h3>
                            <p class="text">Look for applicable discounts such as No Claim Bonus (NCB), long-term policy benefits, or online‑only savings, wherever available. These can help reduce your overall premium.</p>

                            <!-- <a href="https://www.icicilombard.com/health-insurance/max-protect-1-crore-health-insurance?opt=max&amp;source=nav" class="know-more-link" target="_blank">Know More</a> -->
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <!-- <p class="text">What’s more, you get quality assurance on the repairs done at the network garage and get home pick-up and drop off your bike at selected locations. For more details, click here. </p> -->
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section-content " id="how-to-reduce-car-premium">
        <div class="il-container">
            <div class="cont-img-block flex-div">
                <div class="cont-block width-50">
                    <h2 class="heading2">How to Reduce Your Car Insurance Premium?  </h2>
                    <p class="text mt-20">No matter which car you drive, there are a few practical ways to help lower your car insurance premium while staying within policy terms and conditions.</p>
                    <ul class="bullet-list mt-20">
                        <li>
                            <p><strong>Choose the Right Policy: </strong> Select a policy that matches your car’s age, usage and requirements. Older cars may not need every optional add‑on, so choosing only what you truly need can help manage costs. </p>
                        </li>
                        <li>
                            <p><strong>Pick an Appropriate IDV: </strong>A lower Insured Declared Value (IDV) can reduce your premium, but it may also reduce the payout during a claim. It’s best to choose an IDV that fairly reflects your car’s current market value. </p>
                        </li>
                        <li>
                            <p><strong>Review Your Add-ons:</strong>Add‑ons can enhance coverage, but each comes at an extra cost. Keep only the add‑ons that remain relevant for your vehicle; remove the ones you no longer need.</p>
                        </li>
                        <li>
                            <p><strong>Use Your No Claim Bonus (NCB):</strong>If you haven’t made a claim in the previous policy year(s), you may be eligible for a No Claim Bonus. This can help reduce your premium at renewal, as per applicable NCB slabs.  </p>
                        </li>
                        <li>
                            <p><strong>Install Approved Safety Devices</strong>Fitting an anti‑theft device approved by ARAI may make you eligible for a small discount on the premium, as per applicable guidelines.</p>
                        </li>
                    </ul>
                </div>
                <div class="img-block">
                    <img data-src="/docs/default-source/assets/marketing/images/motor-fw-revamp/how_to_reduce_your_car_insurance_premium.webp" alt="How to Reduce Car Insurance Premium?" title="Tips to Reduce Car Insurance Premium" class="lazy ">
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section-content bg-warmgray" id="What-is-NCB-in-car">
        <div class="il-container">
            <h2 class="heading2 align-center">What is No Claim Bonus (NCB)?</h2>
            <p class="sub-txt width-90 align-center"> <a class="link" href="/motor-insurance/car-insurance/no-claim-bonus" target="_blank">No Claim Bonus (NCB) in Car Insurance </a>  is basically your reward for safe driving. If you don’t raise any claims during a policy year, you earn a discount on your premium at the time of renewal.</p>
              <p class="sub-txt width-90 align-center">Do keep in mind - this discount applies only to the own damage part of your car insurance and not the third-party premium. </p>
            <p class="sub-txt width-90 mt-20 align-center strong-txt">Here are different NCB slabs:</p>
            <div class="table-wrapper table-style1  width-80 mt-30">
                <table class="table-wrap">
                    <thead>
                        <tr>
                            <th style="width: 50%">Scenario</th>
                            <th style="width: 50%">Discount Percentage (Applicable Only on Own Damage Premium)</th>
                        </tr>
                    </thead>
                    <tbody>
                        <tr>
                            <td class="strong-txt" style="width: 50%">No claims in the first year </td>
                            <td style="width: 50%">20%</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td class="strong-txt">No claims in the second year</td>
                            <td>25%</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td class="strong-txt">No claims in the third year</td>
                            <td>35%</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td class="strong-txt">No claims in the fourth year</td>
                            <td>45%</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td class="strong-txt">No claims in the fifth year</td>
                            <td>50%</td>
                        </tr>
                    </tbody>
                </table>
            </div>
            <div class="width-90">
                <p class="align-center mt-20  sub-txt">One of the biggest advantages of NCB is that it helps you save on premiums without reducing your coverage. For instance, let’s say your Own Damage premium is ₹10,000 and your Third-party premium is ₹2,094. If you’ve earned an NCB of 45% after four consecutive claim-free years, your discount would be ₹4,500. </p>
                <p class="align-center mt-10  sub-txt">So, your final payable premium (excluding GST) would come to ₹10,000 - ₹4,500 + ₹2,094 = ₹7,594. </p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section-content  bg-sec-blue payuse-section" id="what-are-pay-plan">
        <div class="il-container">
            <h2 class="heading2 align-center">What are Pay As You Use &amp; Pay How You Use Plans?</h2>
            <p class="text align-center mt-20">ICICI Lombard’s Telematics Cover is a usage-based add-on designed to help you reduce your car insurance premiums. It comes with two plans, Pay As You Use and Pay How You Use, and they are applicable to the own damage component of your car
                insurance policy.</p>


            <div class="cards">

                <!-- Card 1 -->
                <div class="card">
                    <h3>Pay As You Use Plan</h3>
                    <ul>
                        <li>It operates on the simple rule that you should pay less car insurance premium if you drive less. </li>
                        <li>It is commonly known as <a class="link" target="_blank" href="/motor-insurance/car-insurance/pay-as-you-drive">Pay As You Drive Cover in Car Insurance</a>.</li>
                        <li>You can opt for 2500, 5000,7500, 10,000 and 15,000 km/year plans depending on your driving needs.</li>
                        <li>You can even top up your insurance coverage if you exceed your plan's kilometres.</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>

                <!-- Card 2 -->
                <div class="card">
                    <h3>Pay How You Use Plan (It rewards customers for their good driving behaviour.)</h3>
                    <ul>
                        <li>Safer drivers receive discounts while riskier driving can attract premium loading.</li>
                        <li>You can get up to 20% discount for having a good driving score.</li>
                        <li>You will get a premium loading of 12% for having a bad driving score.</li>
                   
                    </ul>
                </div>

            </div>

            <p class="text align-center mt-20">
               Since standard car insurance premiums depend on geography, make-model, age of the vehicle and are not based on their usage, most car owners who opted for Telematics add-on save on their premiums.
            </p>
        </div>
    </section>

