    "@type": "Question",
    "name": "What are the risks covered by Private Car Package Insurance Policy?",
    "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "A Private Car Package Policy or comprehensive car insurance offers coverage for both own damages and third-party liabilities. The covered risks include accidents, theft, natural and man-made calamities, fire, third-party property damages and liabilities."
    }
  },{
    "@type": "Question",
    "name": "I am the car's second owner and want to book a fresh policy in my name. What is the process?",
    "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "You need to first transfer the ownership of the car in the registration certificate. Once this is done, you can buy a new car insurance policy under your name."
    }
  },{
    "@type": "Question",
    "name": "Can I switch to ICICI Lombard at the time of renewal from another insurer?",
    "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "Yes, you can easily port your car insurance policy without losing your accumulated NCB."
    }
  },{
    "@type": "Question",
    "name": "What is an endorsement in car insurance?",
    "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "An endorsement is written evidence of an agreed change in the car insurance policy. It is a document that incorporates changes in the policy terms."
    }
  },{
    "@type": "Question",
    "name": "Where can I check my car insurance policy details?",
    "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "You can check all your car insurance details in your policy documents. You can also log in to our website or IL TakeCare app to check the below details:

Policy number
Policy start and end date
Policy type (Comprehensive/OD only/TP only)
Engine & chassis number"
    }
  },{
    "@type": "Question",
    "name": "What is third party liability cover in a car insurance?",
    "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "It covers losses to a third person caused by your insured car. Specifically, it covers:

Any permanent injury/death to a person caused by your insured vehicle
Any damage caused to the property of some other individual, by your insured vehicle"
    }
  },{
    "@type": "Question",
    "name": "What is Zero Depreciation Cover in a car insurance policy?",
    "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "Zero Depreciation Cover is a car insurance add-on that protects you from bearing the cost of depreciation on car parts during a claim. Usually, when you file a claim, the insurer deducts depreciation from the value of the parts that are repaired or replaced, and you end up paying that amount out of your pocket. With Zero Depreciation Cover, the insurer covers this depreciation cost, ensuring you receive a higher claim amount and significantly reducing your out‑of‑pocket expenses."
    }
  },{
    "@type": "Question",
    "name": "What is covered under Zero Depreciation?",
    "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "Zero Depreciation add-on covers the repair and replacement costs of fiber part, rubber, batteries, airbags, nylon and plastic parts, denting, painting, and fiber glass as per policy terms and conditions."
    }
  },{
    "@type": "Question",
    "name": "Do we cover engine in Zero Depreciation?",
    "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "Yes, we do. However, this coverage is only applicable in case of accidental damage to the engine. You can opt for the Engine Protect Plus add-on if you want coverage for consequential losses to the engine."
    }
  },{
    "@type": "Question",
    "name": "What is Engine Protect Plus?",
    "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "It is a car insurance add-on that covers the cost of repairing or replacing an engine, which was damaged due to water ingression/leakage of lubricating oil."
    }
  },{
    "@type": "Question",
    "name": "What is Key Protect cover in car insurance?",
    "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "It is an add-on that covers your car keys and locks against theft or damage. The Key Protect add-on pays for repair or replacement of lost or damaged keys and locks, including locksmith charges. You can opt for this cover in your policy by paying a nominal additional premium."
    }
  },{
    "@type": "Question",
    "name": "What is Garage Cash cover?",
    "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "Garage Cash is an add-on that offers pay a fixed daily allowance when your car is under repair in an authorised garage after an accident. You can use it for alternative transport. Please refer to the policy wordings for terms and conditions."
    }
  },{
    "@type": "Question",
    "name": "Does the ICICI Lombard car insurance policy cover partial theft?",
    "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "Yes, we cover both complete and partial theft under a car insurance policy's own damage section (subject to terms and conditions)."
    }
  },{
    "@type": "Question",
    "name": "Do you cover rat bites in the policy?",
    "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "Yes, we do cover rat bites as per terms and conditions."
    }
  },{
    "@type": "Question",
    "name": "Do you cover damage due to a hit by a coconut or cricket bat?",
    "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "Yes, we do."
    }
  },{
    "@type": "Question",
    "name": "Are passengers covered under car insurance?",
    "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "Only if you have bought an additional Personal Accident Cover for passengers."
    }
  },{
    "@type": "Question",
    "name": "Does car insurance cover natural disasters like floods and earthquakes?",
    "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "Yes, car insurance covers"
    }
  },{
    "@type": "Question",
    "name": "What factors affect my premium amount?",
    "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "Your car insurance premium is impacted by your vehicle’s IDV, age, geographical location, make and model, fuel type, claim history and add-ons opted."
    }
  },{
    "@type": "Question",
    "name": "What is IDV (Insured Declared Value) in a car insurance policy?",
    "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "IDV is your car’s market value after depreciation. It is one of the key factors that determines your claim payout."
    }
  },{
    "@type": "Question",
    "name": "How is the Insured Declared Value (IDV) of my vehicle decided and how does it impact my coverage?",
    "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "IDV is calculated using the manufacturer’s list price minus depreciation (based on the vehicle’s age). It affects both your premium and the maximum amount you can receive in case of total loss or theft."
    }
  },{
    "@type": "Question",
    "name": "What is the meaning of deductible in a car insurance policy?",
    "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "Deductible is the amount you pay during a claim before the insurer settles the rest."
    }
  },{
    "@type": "Question",
    "name": "Is there any discount on the car insurance premium if I install an anti-theft alarm and locking system?",
    "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "Yes, insurers generally provide upto 2.5% discount on car insurance premium for installing approved anti-theft devices."
    }
  },{
    "@type": "Question",
    "name": "Is my No Claim Bonus (NCB) transferable?",
    "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "You cannot transfer your accumulated NCB to someone else. However, you can retain your NCB even after porting your car insurance policy."
    }
  },{
    "@type": "Question",
    "name": "Will my NCB be impacted if I claim for Loss of Personal Belongings & Key Protect add-ons?",
    "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "No."
    }
  },{
    "@type": "Question",
    "name": "Can I reduce my premium by opting for a voluntary deductible?",
    "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "Yes, opting for a higher deductible lowers your car insurance premium but it also increases your out-of-pocket expenses during claims"
    }
  },{
    "@type": "Question",
    "name": "Why should I notify my claim to the insurer directly?",
    "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "It ensure faster claim processing and avoid rejection of admissible claims. If intimate the claim with us before going to the garage, you can get these benefits at our certified preferred garages:

Quick survey
Quality assuranceI for repairs done under claim for 24 months or 10000 km, whichever is earlier
Complimentary vehicle body wash
Complimentary sanitisation - on major touchpoints
Complimentary towing at the time of the accident"
    }
  },{
    "@type": "Question",
    "name": "How do I register my claim?",
    "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "You can file a car insurance claim online via our website , through the IL TakeCare app, or by calling the toll-free number 1800 2666 or contacting us on WhatsApp: 7738282666."
    }
  },{
    "@type": "Question",
    "name": "What is a cashless claim and a non-cashless/reimbursement claim?",
    "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "Under the cashless claim facility, we pay our share of the vehicle repair charges directly to the garage, provided the vehicle is repaired in our network garage. Whereas if the vehicle is repaired in a garage outside our network's purview, you will have to pay the repair charges to the garage. You can get your claim amount reimbursed by submitting the original bills and payment receipts to our office."
    }
  },{
    "@type": "Question",
    "name": "How many times can we claim under car insurance in a year?",
    "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "You can make any number of claims in the year."
    }
  },{
    "@type": "Question",
    "name": "What documents are required to file a car insurance claim?",
    "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "Some of important documents required to file a car insurance claim include RC, driving licence, FIR (if applicable), claim form and repair bills."
    }
  },{
    "@type": "Question",
    "name": "Why can a car insurance claim be rejected?",
    "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "Your claim can be rejected due to multiple reasons, including policy lapse, misrepresentation or illegal driving."
    }
  },{
    "@type": "Question",
    "name": "When should I renew car insurance?",
    "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "You need to renew car insurance before it expires, so that there is no break in coverage. In case of a gap between expiry and renewal, you may lose out on claims and your accumulated NCB."
    }
  },{
    "@type": "Question",
    "name": "I am an existing ICICI Lombard customer. Can I renew my car insurance policy online?",
    "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "You, can renew your car insurance policy by visiting our website."
    }
  },{
    "@type": "Question",
    "name": "Can I renew my car insurance after expiry?",
    "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "Ideally, you should renew your car insurance policy before expiry of the previous policy. In case your vehicle insurance policy has already expired, our authorised surveyor would require an inspection of the car, before policy issuance. The policy would only be issued subject to satisfactory inspection and submission of required documents."
    }
  },{
    "@type": "Question",
    "name": "Is inspection required if my car insurance policy has expired?",
    "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "Yes."
    }
  },{
    "@type": "Question",
    "name": "Where can I get a duplicate copy of my car insurance policy?",
    "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "You can download the PDF version of your car insurance policy via our IL TakeCare App."
    }
  },{
    "@type": "Question",
    "name": "What do I do with my car insurance policy if I sell my car?",
    "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "You can transfer your car insurance to the new owner."
    }
  },{
    "@type": "Question",
    "name": "How can I transfer car insurance to the buyer of my car?",
    "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "You can transfer your car insurance to the new owner."
    }
  }]
}
